{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-template-tsx","path":"/posts/i-wont-be-commanded/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"id":"a523e1fb-cb48-5a0f-9ccd-9def348443e4","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>I will not be commanded\nI will not be controlled\nI will not let my future go on, without the help of my soul\n<em>Greg Holden, “The Lost Boy”</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<div style=\"max-width: 400px; margin: 0 auto;\">\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 960px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/68947a6f595f63cbe7b9539caec0462f/71c1d/image1.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 66.66666666666666%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/68947a6f595f63cbe7b9539caec0462f/8ac56/image1.webp 240w,\n/static/68947a6f595f63cbe7b9539caec0462f/d3be9/image1.webp 480w,\n/static/68947a6f595f63cbe7b9539caec0462f/e46b2/image1.webp 960w,\n/static/68947a6f595f63cbe7b9539caec0462f/f992d/image1.webp 1440w,\n/static/68947a6f595f63cbe7b9539caec0462f/0abaa/image1.webp 1536w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/68947a6f595f63cbe7b9539caec0462f/8ff5a/image1.png 240w,\n/static/68947a6f595f63cbe7b9539caec0462f/e85cb/image1.png 480w,\n/static/68947a6f595f63cbe7b9539caec0462f/d9199/image1.png 960w,\n/static/68947a6f595f63cbe7b9539caec0462f/07a9c/image1.png 1440w,\n/static/68947a6f595f63cbe7b9539caec0462f/71c1d/image1.png 1536w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/68947a6f595f63cbe7b9539caec0462f/d9199/image1.png\"\n            alt=\"A vintage brass compass resting in an open palm on weathered wood\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n</div>\n<p>I keep coming back to this song. Three lines describe something most of us forget. You can lose your own voice without noticing.</p>\n<p>People change their tone to be accepted. They soften an opinion they actually hold. They stay quiet not because they have nothing to say, but because what they want to say might offend someone.</p>\n<p>Over time, the edits become the voice. The original one gets harder to find.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-patterns\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#the-patterns\" aria-label=\"the patterns permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>The Patterns</h2>\n<p>The patterns are familiar. Agreeing in a meeting to avoid conflict. Holding back an idea to avoid the spotlight. Being the reliable yes sir who never pushes back.</p>\n<p>From the outside it looks like cooperation. From the inside, you stop knowing where the politeness ends and you begin.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-authenticity-comes-first\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#why-authenticity-comes-first\" aria-label=\"why authenticity comes first permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Why Authenticity Comes First</h2>\n<p>Authenticity is the precondition for speaking freely. If you’re afraid to speak, you’re already editing. And the voice in the room is no longer yours. It’s a version tuned for someone else’s comfort.</p>\n<p>Call it politeness for a while. Do it long enough and you stop knowing what you actually believe. Offending someone now and then costs less than losing track of what you think.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-i-mean-by-soul\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#what-i-mean-by-soul\" aria-label=\"what i mean by soul permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>What I Mean by Soul</h2>\n<p>The word can sound religious. I don’t use it that way. The soul is your conscience, your values, your sense of meaning. It’s the inner voice that knows what you believe before you translate it for someone else.</p>\n<p>“Without the help of my soul” is a refusal to live by external commands. It’s the choice to let that inner voice guide your future instead. A future built without it isn’t really yours. It belongs to the people who won’t live it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-practice\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#the-practice\" aria-label=\"the practice permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>The Practice</h2>\n<p>The lyric isn’t asking you to be loud or difficult. It’s asking you not to be commanded, not to be controlled, not to let your future move forward without that inner voice.</p>\n<p>So I keep coming back to a small instruction. Just be you. Say the thing. Hold the opinion. Disagree when you actually disagree. Authenticity isn’t a trait. It’s a practice. It’s loyalty, and you owe it to yourself first.</p>\n<p>Before I agree, before I shrink, before I say the easier thing, I ask whether the answer has my soul in it. If it doesn’t, it isn’t really mine. And it isn’t really my life.</p>\n<p>I won’t be commanded. I won’t be controlled. Just be you.</p>","timeToRead":2,"fields":{"slug":"/posts/2026-04-29---i-wont-be-commanded//posts/i-wont-be-commanded","tagSlugs":["/tag/personal-development/","/tag/authenticity/","/tag/mindset/","/tag/life-tips/"]},"frontmatter":{"date":"2026-04-29T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["Personal Development","Authenticity","Mindset","Life Tips"],"title":"I Won't Be Commanded, I Won't Be Controlled","description":"A song that keeps reminding me to be loyal to my own voice. Why authenticity is the precondition for speaking freely.","socialImage":{"publicURL":"/static/68947a6f595f63cbe7b9539caec0462f/image1.png"}}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/posts/2026-04-29---i-wont-be-commanded//posts/i-wont-be-commanded"}},"staticQueryHashes":["4208939363"],"slicesMap":{}}